  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The prossimo passage",
   "texto": [
    "The **passato prossimo** is often used to count something finished. With many verbs it is formed with the present of **avere** + the **participio**: **Ho mangiato** (ate / have eaten). Natural translation depends on the context.",
    "Regular practice for the participle: **-are → -ato** (mangiare → mangiato), **-ere → -uto** (sell → bandage), **-ire → -ito** (sleep → sleeping). There are many frequent irregular participles, which are learned on a case-by-case basis."
   ]
  },
